  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The build, the 39 tests and the architecture check all pass.\n\nA straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume this event in other repos. ARCH-4 says renames go through deprecation.\n\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`) and `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`). The old two are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected event in `test/app.test.ts` and added assertions for the new fields in `test/adapters.test.ts`.\n\nI left the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the legacy export unchanged. ARCH-8 requires the response to stay backward compatible, and your request only covered the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, you'd first need to confirm both consumers have moved to the new names. After that, a follow-up change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. I can also add the deprecation note to the README if you want it.",
